    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d894">

                <pb facs="0959" n="1793" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/263</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">DeBillier</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-27T16:00:00-04:42">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s March 23, 7 p.m. Given positive assurances orally that no
                    distinction will be made between Dutch boats and those referred to in Embassy’s
                    despatch No. 247, October 12, 1917. Promised confirmatory note tomorrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">DeBillier</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
